1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A few drops of colored fluid under
the front of your engine isn't
always the radiator.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Water pumps have a tiny weep hole
built in — it's designed to leak a
little before it fails.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
That hole lets coolant escape early,
instead of the seal blowing out with
no warning.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,000
One clue: it's colored and sticky —
not clear water like AC condensation.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
You might also see a dried, crusty
residue trail near the pump before a
puddle ever shows up.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Ignore it long enough and the engine
can overheat with no warning.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Stop by and we'll take a look.
